[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_1]
Report 14-A.0b

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_1_desc]
Subject: Manehattan Business Alliance

Security Department Special Agent Investigation Report: The Manehattan Business Alliance led by Gladmane is a commercial group that operates real estate, luxury goods, and consumer goods on the surface, but in fact, it makes huge profits by collecting protection fees, smuggling and trading electric energy products, and looting and selling magic energy products.

As the investigation deepens, darker facts emerge: under the guise of “business transactions”, the gangs under the Business Alliance are engaged in slave trading, including both exporting and importing slaves.

Security Department special agents are planning a series of actions: when we obtain evidence, we only need to make it public, and the illegal empire government of Cozy Glow will have no choice but to make a statement under public pressure.

The next report is expected to be sent in a month.

Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_1_o0]
Any details about the slave trade?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_1_o1]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_2]
The Story of Big Bucks

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_2_desc]
When Gladmane was still running the Las Pegasus resort, Big Bucks was a magician who parterned with Jack Pot to perform magic shows at the resort. When the Flim Flam brothers took over the resort and Gladmane fled to Manehattan, the two magicians stayed in Las Pegasus and continued to perform magic.
Unfortunately, the Ultimate Battle has caused a lot of damage to the resort, and fewer and fewer ponies have the spare money to watch magic shows, so the two magicians’ income is getting lower and lower. Jack Pot still insists on performing magic, while Big Bucks becomes a train driver to transport supplies for the Flim Flam brothers. The extremely low salary made Big Bucks have the idea of smuggling to Manehattan. Big Bucks heard about the wealth of Manehattan, and also heard that the former boss Gladmane had achieved some success there, so he brought his lifelong savings and wanted to see the paper-drunk gold in Manehattan.
The Las Pegasus in 1000’s Spring was under strict temporary control, but Big Bucks’ job as a train driver gave him the opportunity. Big Bucks planned to secretly take Jack Pot with him to escape Las Pegasus while transporting supplies to Manehattan.
Unfortunately, the train driven by Big Bucks encountered an accident on the way, and Big Bucks as the driver also became the culprit. In the end, Big Bucks forged his own death and escaped to Manehattan with a new identity. But what Big Bucks didn’t expect was that the moment he arrived in Manehattan, he was caught by the local mafia. The mafia quickly saw through Big Bucks’ false identity and used it to coerce Big Bucks to do things for them.
The mafia boss seemed a little surprised that Big Bucks could report Gladmane’s name, but this did not seem to change Big Bucks’ fate. The story afterwards is not very clear. The last time other ponies ever heard Big Bucks’ name was on another train. The train was heading to a mine on the border of the Equestria Empire. The mine was operated by the Gladmane Group. The ponies working there had no salary and were forced to work by the forepony. It was said that few ponies have come back from there. And Big Buck’s story ends here.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_2_o0]
Wait, a train driver?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_3]
Not an Isolated Case - Manehattan Slave Trade Secret Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_3_desc]
Subject: Manehattan Slave Trade

The following is the Security Department special agent’s investigation report on the slave trade:
Slave Acquisition: Gladmane’s mafia employs a diverse range of methods to procure slaves, including coercion, deception, and brute force. Gold coins, crystals, muffins or even rubber chickens are all used as a trap to lure unsuspecting victims.
Slave Transportation: Gladmane’s mafia utilizes networks of hidden tunnels, secret passages, magically concealed carriages, ordinary carriages, scrap carriages, or even walking to whisk away slaves across Manehattan, like a covert Wonderbolts operation.
Slave Exploitation: Slaves acquired by Gladmane’s mafia are allocated to various industries throughout Manehattan, including factories, construction sites, mines and even high-profile establishments like theaters, casinos, and stock quantitative trading firms (although we don’t understand why slaves are allocated to these places).
Control and Security: Gladmane’s mafia has insidiously infiltrated key positions within Manehattan’s law enforcement agencies: police chief, deputy chief, chief’s secretary, chief’s secretary’s secretary, deputy chief’s secretary, head of the task force, ordinary police officers, janitors, and janitors’ dogs. This allows them to maintain layers of protection and evade legal sanctions.
Public Perception: The mafia manipulates public perception through a combination of fear, misinformation, and carefully crafted narratives. For example, in response to rumors that “three slave earth ponies were spotted being transported on the streets of Manehattan by eyewitnesses yesterday”, they would promptly refute it: “This is a pure lie. Nothing happened yesterday. There were more than three ponies at the scene, they were not earth ponies, they were not being transported, and they were not on the streets.”

The next report is expected to be sent in half a month.

Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_3_o0]
Can you prove that the illegal empire is involved?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_3_o1]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_4]
Report 14-A.2a

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_4_desc]
Subject: Manehattan and the illegal empire

As early as the coronation ceremony of Cozy Glow, Gladmane had already begun to deeply participate in the political decision-making of the central government of the Equestria Empire.

It is rumored that Gladmane participated in a secret meeting in Canterlot around the time of the coronation, and the main topic of the meeting was the resolution to establish the Equestria Empire Ministry of Order. Or, to put it bluntly, Gladmane is the actual founder of the Ministry of Order, and only he can propose the idea of implementing a series of terrifying measures such as monitoring and reviewing all ponies.

Evidence shows that although Gladmane has no direct connection with the Equestria Empire government and the Ministry of Order on the surface, he is still the biggest partner behind the Ministry of Order. In fact, in the slave trade conducted by Manehattan, a considerable number of slaves, and even some of Gladmane’s trusted subordinates, have been sent to Canterlot to become employees of the Ministry of Order. It is precisely because of the Ministry of Order’s huge demand for labor that Canterlot can turn a blind eye to what is happening in Manehattan.

Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_4_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5]
Empire condemns Manehattan for Slave Trade

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_desc]
As the Manehattan slave trade was exposed in recent days, the voices calling for the central government of the Empire to respond to this issue have also increased. This morning, Empress Cozy Glow issued a notice:
“The Equestria Empire is committed to uniting all ponies and building a country where ponies can live a happy and stable life. The slave trade is an unacceptable behavior of the Empire...”
“Therefore, the central government of the Empire is highly concerned about the relevant information and requires Manehattan and its surrounding areas to rectify immediately. Before the rectification is completed, the special license of Gladmane Group will be cancelled, and the mayor of Gladmane will be suspended...”
“However, the historical issues are complicated. Manehattan and its surrounding areas have long enjoyed a high degree of autonomy. In the spirit of unity and friendship, the Empire will not destroy this autonomous tradition, nor will it interfere with the internal affairs of Manehattan and its surrounding areas that do not involve slave trade, and will not station troops in Manehattan...”
In response to this statement, the leader of the Resistance, Starlight Glimmer, believes that this is a very ambiguous disclaimer, while the Equestria Empire News believes that it reflects the Empire’s sense of responsibility and emphasizes the need to prevent some particular forces from taking advantage of the situation to discredit the Empire.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_o0]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_o2]
Cope!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_o3]
Cope!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_5_o4]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6]
The Resistance Defeated the Business Alliance

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6_desc]
News from Our Town: the Resistance army has defeated the security forces of the Manehattan Business Alliance and has occupied several cities of the Business Alliance, including Manehattan, Trottingham, and Fillydelphia. It is reported that the former mayor of Manehattan, Gladmane, is currently missing, and the Manehattan Business Alliance has fundamentally collapsed.

The leader of the Resistance, Starlight Glimmer, declared that she would “liberate all ponies enslaved under Gladmane’s rule and eliminate the gang forces”. Empress Cozy Glow of the Equestria Empire called this “a serious violation of the sovereignty of the Empire committed by the rebels” and sent more troops to the east of Equestria. Trixie, Duchess of Ponyville, militarily occupied Baltimare under the pretext of “protecting local citizens”. Currently, the Resistance has controlled the entire territory of the Business Alliance except for the southern cities.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6_o0]
These thugs!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6_o1]
Freedom forever!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6_o2]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_6_o3]
Congratulations!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7]
Eastern Equestria Cities’ Summit

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7_desc]
After the liberation of Manehattan, Starlight Glimmer invited representatives from various districts of Eastern Equestria to attend a meeting in Equality Town to make the cities of Eastern Equestria more united.

Representatives from Trottingham, Hooflyn, Manehattan, and Fillydelphia attended the meeting, but Baltimare was absent because it was not under the control of the Liberation Front. At the meeting, Starlight Glimmer strongly condemned the “criminals harbored by Ponyville” and said that Ponyville would “pay the price”. The representatives of the cities present expressed their support.

It is reported that the Empire has sent more troops to its eastern border, and stated that the Ponyville should be prepared to fight against the Liberation Front, claiming that “Ponyville’s actions are protecting the citizens of the Empire”. Ponyville has not yet made a formal response.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7_o1]
Traitors! Clowns!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7_o2]
Unity!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_7_o3]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_8]
Eastern Equestria Cities’ Summit

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_8_desc]
After the resolution of the slave trade problem in Manehattan, Starlight Glimmer invited representatives of various interest groups from cities in Eastern Equestria to attend a summit in Manehattan to discuss the future development of Eastern Equestria.
A total of 9 city representatives attended the meeting: 2 from the Liberation Front, 1 from Hooflyn, 1 from Farrier Hill, 2 from Manehattan, 1 from Fillydelphia, 1 from Baltimare, and 1 from Horseshoe Bay.
Although the Liberation Front had only two representatives at the meeting, since Hooflyn and Farrier Hill were also under the control of the Liberation Front, and Baltimare was slightly pro-Liberation Front, the Liberation Front already had a majority at the meeting.
However, the representatives of Fillydelphia, Manehattan, and Horseshoe Bay, as important portal and commercial cities in Eastern Equestria that could sit on an equal footing with Manehattan, showed strong dissatisfaction at the meeting. They believed that the Liberation Front’s equatism policy had seriously damaged their interests. They did not want to have disputes with the Equestria Empire. Meanwhile, Baltimare showed a neutral attitude at the meeting.
In the end, the proposal put forward by the Liberation Front was deadlocked with 4 votes in favor, 1 abstention, and 4 votes against. The representatives of the three cities did not dare to openly oppose Starlight Glimmer at the meeting, but their attitude had already indicated their position. If we did not get their support, the proposal would be nothing more than a piece of paper that could never be passed.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_8_o0]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_8_o1]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_9]
Operation <=Manehattan Dawn=>

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_9_desc]
Report to our great leader Starlight Glimmer: We are looking for Gladmane’s killer all over Eastern Equestria, but no pony is willing to do it.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_9_o0]
Why would you report that?!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_10]
Operation <=Manehattan Dawn=>

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_10_desc]
This morning, the CEO of the Manehattan Group, Gladmane, went to the suburbs of Manehattan to inspect an underground casino — literally, it is hidden in a basement of a street store.
However, Gladmane felt something was wrong as soon as he got off the car — his bodyguards did not walk into the store with him, but stopped at the door. Gladmane’s intuition told him that this inspection might be unusual.
But Gladmane’s intuition obviously came a little late — a hoofgonne had already aimed at him. “Say hello to my sisterr”, said a pony who walked out of the shadows. Gladmane saw clearly that this was the captain of his bodyguards.
“Sister? I don’t know your sister!”
“Exactly, you don’t know her. She was taken away because of your slave trade.”
“No way, the gang has rules, you know it. We never kidnap our fellow ——”
Well, Gladmane didn’t have more chance to defend himself.

§b“Well done, comrades! This is a very clever move!”§!
§b“Uh... Sorry to ... report to our great leader Starlight Glimmer that... this is not arranged by us...”§!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_10_o0]
Huh?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_11]
Breaking News: Former Mayor of Manehattan Assassinated!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_11_desc]
Yesterday, the former mayor of Manehattan and CEO of the Gladmane Group, Gladmane, was murdered in a clothing store.
The murderer was his head of security, who has killed himself at the scene. The motive for the crime is suspected to be a personal conflict with Gladmane.
Stay tuned to this newspaper for more details.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_11_o0]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_12]
Liberation

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_12_desc]
Starlight Glimmer is on the train, holding a newspaper in her hooves, and the headline on top is:

“Manehattan Liberated”

Well, the purpose of her trip is exactly to go to Manehattan to inspect and announce the victory of the resistance to the world. The train departs from Northern Hooflyn and heads southeast, crossing the bridge to Manehattan. The Manehattan gangs didn’t dare to blow up the bridge, and the railway on it has been repaired and put into use. After crossing the bridge and moving forward, it is the station of Manehattan.

Starlight Glimmer walks on the streets outside Manehattan. The city’s outskirts, under the operation of the Leshan Group, have turned from residential areas into slums. The street barricades that have not been removed, the bullet marks on the houses around, and the uneven road surface all indicate that there has been a fierce battle here. On the side of the road, the ponies of the Army Department are maintaining order, and the ponies of the National Security Department are dragging ponies with more or less connections with the gang to the temporary detention point in the suburbs.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_12_o0]
The Metropolis is now Free

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_12_TOOLTIP]
§YFocus Tree§! updated

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_13]
Report 12-A.0a

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_13_desc]
Subject: Resistance Status Report (Winter 1002)

Currently, the Resistance is still surrounded by the illegal empire. At the same time, some refugees have fled from the illegal empire and entered the Resistance-controlled area in the border areas where the illegal empire’s control is weak, but the scale is small. It is expected that the trend of refugees entering the Resistance will not stop until the Empire strengthens border control.
The Resistance’s production is threatened. Under the economic blockade and the influence of refugees, the Resistance can only concentrate resources in the town of Equality and several important strongholds. In addition, the reconnaissance Pegasus of the Cloudsdale and the border patrol of the illegal empire have repeatedly attacked the transportation routes with an average frequency of 12 times a day, and the Economic Department has to allocate some resources to protect the material transportation.
The construction of the Resistance’s defense system has made some progress. The defense positions in the town of Equality and the surrounding areas are basically complete. There are problems with the exploration route from Equality Town to the eastern wasteland, which is easy to be attacked. It is recommended to add checkpoints along the route and increase the equipment route.
Our military strength is currently severely restricted. In the case of production being attacked, military production is difficult to carry out on a large scale. At the same time, there are risks of exposure in the training and expansion of legions, which may leak military deployment intelligence, so large-scale military reforms should not be carried out.

National Security Department’s assessment of security level (A-E): C
Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_13_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_14]
Report 12-A.1a

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_14_desc]
Subject: World Situation Report (Winter 1002)

Manehattan: The Manehattan controlled by the Manehattan Gang of Gladmane, on the surface, is a city of economic prosperity and rapid commercial development, but in fact, the local gap between the rich and the poor is extremely significant. The number of refugees exiled from Manehattan is 20% more than that from the Empire. According to local informants, there are abnormal large-scale population movements in Manehattan, yet the specific situation is unknown.
Crystal Empire: The Crystal Empire is a de facto colony of Cozy Glow and Queen Chrysalis. The Crystal Empire practices limited democracy. In fact, the Canterlot and Changeling delegations almost control half of the Crystal Empire Council, while the Royals, as the legitimate rulers of the local government, only control the other half. It is worth noting that there is great potential for democratization movements in the area, and there is a possibility of persuading Flurry Heart to cooperate. With appropriate intervention, there is a possibility of a large-scale democratic movement in the area, or even an independence war.
Equestria Empire (illegal): The illegal empire has become a mess. Due to Cozy Glow’s lack of power to control the entire Empire, Canterlot’s actual controlled territory only accounts for half of all areas obedient to the Empire, and the rest are autonomous territories granted by Cozy Glow. Some autonomous territories have greater autonomy, and they only superficially obey Canterlot, while in fact forming a competitive situation with Canterlot.
Changelings: The Changelings and the illegal empire have conflicting interests. The alliance of the “Big Three” is almost in name only, and Tirek is no longer concerned with Equestrian affairs. The conflict of interests between the Changelings and the Empire is particularly evident in the Crystal Empire. It is expected that when one side of the two parties falls into difficulties, the other side will not provide substantial assistance, which is beneficial to the Resistance.

Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_14_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_15]
The Day of Contact

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_15_desc]
Every mid-month, Starlight, Discord, and Sunset will contact each other to exchange their information.
Thanks to the existence of the magical diary, it is very convenient for Starlight and Sunset to contact each other. Starlight picked up the notebook and wrote down the contact content on the paper:
“We are currently short of supplies, and refugees come to Our Town every day...”
The magical traces on the notebook ensure that Sunset has received the contact content.

Putting down the notebook, Starlight looked at the clock. Sunburst pushed the door open and walked in.
“Sunburst, hasn’t Discord replied yet?”
“No, um... I think the messenger seems to have been caught by the illegal empire on the way? After all, Discord’s animals never deliver messages late...”
Starlight had long anticipated this situation. Since the cut-off of land contact, Starlight and Discord could only communicate through messengers. The messengers not only had to evade the search of the illegal empire, but sometimes they also had to cross mountains and ridges, resulting in extremely unsmooth information exchange routes between the two sides.
Starlight sighed:
“Every time a message is sent, we may lose a pony. We are simply sending ponies to their deaths. Sunburst, let the messenger send the message for the last time on the next Day of Contact, one to Sunset and one to Discord.”
“What for?”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_15_o0]
“... Bring the radio over.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_16]
Another Year

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_16_desc]
“Another year has come, and the resistance is still alive. Cheers!”
“To victory!” §b“To victory!”§!
“To friendship!” §b“To friendship!”§!
“To liberation!” §b“To liberation!”§!
“To cheating!” §b“To... what?”§!

“To cheating!Yes, I’m talking about you! Friendship is magic, but friendship is not omnipotent. The console is omnipotent, but the console is not friendship.”
“Don’t look at others, I’m talking about you! For the love of Celestia, shame on you!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_16_o0]
The End

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_17]
Friendship is Snapped

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_17_desc]
Starlight Glimmer had a dream. She dreamed that her friends were swallowed by darkness and were getting farther and farther away from her, and she could only watch all this happen without being able to do anything. The dream was so real that Starlight Glimmer woke up at six in the morning, two hours earlier than usual.

Through the window of her room, Starlight saw an unexpected sight: at six in the morning, when the sky was not yet bright, all the ponies in town seemed to have gathered in front of the newspaper office. No matter which pony, there was a look of sadness or resentment on their faces, and there was even an incredibly bright rainbow hanging in the sky in the direction of Canterlot.

This is definitely not normal, Starlight Glimmer thought. Before she could leave, Sunburst burst into the room almost breaking the door. “Starlight, oh my goodness, look at this!”

Starlight suddenly had a bad feeling, she picked up the newspaper Sunburst gave her and read it:

“Jahr Null: To celebrate the defeat of Twilight Sparkle and her anti-harmony group by the forces of justice, Empress Cozy Glow, Queen Chrysalis and Lord Tirek decided to replace the ‘Hearth’s Warming Eve’ of the Celestia era with ‘Jahr Null’, celebrating the establishment of true harmonic order. On the eve of Jahr Null, the anti-harmony elements were brought to justice. Twilight Sparkle and her five accomplices have been permanently stripped of their identities and transferred to an undisclosed location for isolated disposition. For reasons of imperial security, their place of confinement and present condition will no longer be made public... What?!” She could hardly believe her eyes.

“No longer public?! Where did they take them?!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_17_o0]
“Sunburst, something terrible happened, write to Discord and Sunset, quickly!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_17_TOOLTIP]
§YFocus Tree§! updated

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_18]
The Lost and the Unforgotten

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_18_desc]
Ever since receiving that devastating news, Starlight Glimmer has been listless every day, often crying uncontrollably when she recalls the memories of the past. Her bloodshot eyes became particularly prominent against the backdrop of her dark circles. Sunburst and Sugar Belle have repeatedly tried to persuade Starlight to cheer up, citing the development of the front and the need for her leadership, but Starlight returned to her listless state after completing the necessary daily tasks.

So, Sunburst decided to pull his old friend out of the mire. One night, as Starlight was about to step into her house, Sunburst stopped her, just as Twilight Sparkle had stopped Starlight Glimmer years ago.

“Starlight Glimmer!” Sunburst steadied himself. “I am also heartbroken about Twilight and the others disappearing, but...”

“But they may already be dead!” Starlight interrupted Sunburst. “The Empire released no records, and no pony knows where they were taken. Three years, and not even a single word from them. For all these years, apart from you, I finally made a few friends and even became headmare of the School of Friendship. But the pony who first taught me friendship, she has already... already...!” Starlight fought back her tears and nearly broke down.

Sunburst sighed. “We do not know whether Twilight Sparkle is still alive, and we cannot accept the Empire’s silence as an answer. She worked so hard to teach you because she hoped you could stand on your own and lead ponies toward the true meaning of friendship. Wherever she may be now, if you step out of this shadow and bring harmony to Equestria again, she would be proud of you.”

“Starlight...” Sunburst reached out his hoof and wiped Starlight’s tears.

“What remains should not be only memories...”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_18_o0]
“The driving force to move forward is your dreams.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_19]
The Speech

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_19_desc]
Ponies gathered in the center of the square. Since the devastating news of “Jahr Null”, the resistance had been in an uproar, eager to rush to Canterlot, capture Empress Cozy Glow, and execute her a thousand times over. Today they gathered in the square, hoping Starlight Glimmer would do something to win justice for their missing friends.

Although Starlight Glimmer still grieved over the silence surrounding her mentor, she understood that she could no longer wait for the Empire to surrender the truth. What she could do now was unite the resistance and prepare for the liberation to come.

“Everypony!” Starlight shouted, and every pony below fell silent. “You have all heard. Twilight Sparkle—our mentor, the Princess of Friendship—has been erased from the world by Cozy Glow. The Empire will not tell us where she is. It will not even prove that she is alive. How dare they?!”

“How dare they?!” The ponies echoed in unison, their emotions running high.

“We do not know whether Twilight Sparkle can still hear us, but her disappearance will not be buried beneath the Empire’s silence! Every pony has seen the evil of the so-called ‘Equestria Empire’. We must unite, find Twilight Sparkle, and make every architect of this crime pay!”

Starlight Glimmer took a deep breath and adjusted her emotions:

“It’s not that we have to do this, it’s that we choose to do this!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_19_o0]
Thunderous applause, from every pony

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_20]
Father’s Letter

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_20_desc]
Dear my beloved daughter,

It has been three years since we last contacted after the war. It was not until recently that I received the horrible news of Princess Twilight’s death that I dared to gather the courage to secretly write a letter to you, I am very sorry for everything.

I believe you must be very sad now, dad understands your feelings very well. After Princess Twilight was defeated, I heard said that you sacrificed yourself to protect Princess Twilight. It was really dark times for me. I was drowning in memories of you every day. Until the news of your uprising made headlines, that was the happiest moment of my life: Even though you became a wanted criminal, even though I was forced to stand on the opposite side of you, all that mattered was that you were still alive.

The reason dad wrote this letter to you is to hope that you can step out of the shadow and gather the courage. The ponies of Equestria must all be hoping that you can lead them to drive away the evil pony in Canterlot Castle. They need your help. Move forward! Princess Twilight will definitely bless you. May you have a bright journey ahead, and your dad in Sire’s Hollow will be waiting for your triumphant return.

By the way, please send my regards to Sunburst. His mother misses him very much, but there are spies everywhere, and it is almost impossible to send out a second letter. I can only ask you to pass on her greetings.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_20_o0]
Starlight framed the letter and read it several times every day from then on

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_21]
Our Town Declaration

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_21_desc]
“Beep——beep——beep——”

“Ponies of Equestria, I am the leader of the resistance, Starlight Glimmer, and I am speaking to all of Equestria from Our Town.”

“Since Celestia, Equestria has been a land full of friendship and harmony, a paradise where earth ponies, pegasi, and unicorns live in harmony. Every pony can remember how peaceful and tranquil life used to be.”

“But this peace and tranquility was shattered three years ago. Cozy Glow and her accomplices tore this land apart, brainwashed the citizens of Equestria with the ridiculous ‘Neo-harmonism’, and dragged the paradise of friendship and harmony into the abyss of discord and strife.”

“Ponies will never forget what Cozy Glow has done. She imprisoned Princess Celestia and Princess Luna, broke the friendship between the three tribes, and made Princess Twilight Sparkle and her friends disappear from the world. She refuses to disclose their whereabouts, hoping Equestria will forget even its right to demand the truth. She destroyed Equestria’s harmony and stole the bright future of its ponies. This will not end here.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_21_o0]
§R“Cozy Glow, you are next.”§!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_22]
Starlight Glimmer made the “Our Town Declaration”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_22_desc]
Today, the leader of the resistance, Starlight Glimmer, has made a speech in Our Town against the Equestria Empire, and the following is an excerpt from the “Our Town Declaration”:
“Beep——beep——beep——”

“Ponies of Equestria, I am the leader of the resistance, Starlight Glimmer, and I am speaking to all of Equestria from Our Town.”

“Since Celestia, Equestria has been a land full of friendship and harmony, a paradise where earth ponies, pegasi, and unicorns live in harmony. Every pony can remember how peaceful and tranquil life used to be.”

“But this peace and tranquility was shattered three years ago. Cozy Glow and her accomplices tore this land apart, brainwashed the citizens of Equestria with the ridiculous ‘Neo-harmonism’, and dragged the paradise of friendship and harmony into the abyss of discord and strife.”

“Ponies will never forget what Cozy Glow has done. She imprisoned Princess Celestia and Princess Luna, broke the friendship between the three tribes, and made Princess Twilight Sparkle and her friends disappear from the world. She refuses to disclose their whereabouts, hoping Equestria will forget even its right to demand the truth. She destroyed Equestria’s harmony and stole the bright future of its ponies. This will not end here.”

“Cozy Glow, you are next.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_22_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_22_o1]
How dare you, rebel scum?!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_22_o2]
March on!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_23]
The Road of Exile

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_23_desc]
Wandering Wind was running in the valley, with two border patrol ponies chasing him.

He used to live in Ponyville and made a living by planting apple trees. Until not long ago the damn Empire sent some ponies to cut down all his trees in order to “meet the Empire’s supply needs”. They even demolished his house and took it back to Canterlot. Wandering Wind wanted to resist, but the riot police hired by Trixie beat him up and threw him on the side of the road. It was then that he made up his mind to escape from Ponyville with a few fellow ponies one night and head to Our Town, where he heard that the resistance was brewing.

Soon after their departure, they ran into a few unicorn thugs who had ill intentions and a little magic left. The thugs chased them like ducks. Wandering Wind and his fellow ponies had to run into the mountains, where a few pegasi thugs threw lightning bolts at them. Some of Wandering Wind’s fellow ponies died, some were injured, and they finally managed to escape the thunderstorm. When they reached the border, Wandering Wind and two other earth pony fellows were all that was left. They cursed the pegasi and unicorns, but bad luck struck again as they ran into the border patrol. The other two earth ponies were caught, and only Wandering Wind managed to escape, by now. They are still chasing him.

Now, two patrol ponies are waving their batons and shouting something at Wandering Wind. He can’t hear them clearly, but he knows those must be bad words. Just as they are about to catch up with him, he is ready to fight to the death. Suddenly, an arrow shoots down from the sky and flies towards the two patrol ponies. A white light corrects the arrow’s trajectory, and it hits one of the patrol ponies right in the head. The other patrol pony is terrified by the sudden attack and runs away.

Wandering Wind escapes death and breathes a sigh of relief, just to see a pegasus and a unicorn in front of him. He remembers his earth pony fellows who were killed, and can’t help but roar in anger, “Damn pegasi and unicorns, you really want to do this again?”

“Wow there, we just saved you, and that’s your reaction?” the unicorn says. The pegasus then speaks up, “Did you see that arrow in the sky? I fired it!”
“Oh come on, if I didn’t correct the trajectory with my magic, you wouldn’t even know where it would hit. Anyway, I’m Magenta Mist, and he’s Fervent Flame. We are ponies of the resistance. You must be a refugee from the Empire, right? We won’t hurt you.”

It seems they really have no ill intentions? Wandering Wind puts down his guard, “Alright, I’m Wandering Wind. Is the resistance up ahead? How do I get to Our Town?”

“Just keep going north, Fervent Flame checked the road yesterday. It’s safe. We live just near Our Town. Come find us if you need anything.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_23_o0]
Heading north, Wandering Wind finally escaped the Empire

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_24]
Report 27-B.0a

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_24_desc]
Subject: Industrial Plan 1003

Currently, the civil industry within the territory of the Resistance can still operate. The labor shortage has been filled by refugees from the illegal empire. The civil industry-related workponies have all completed basic anti-raid training. The destructive power to the civil industry caused by the raids of the illegal empire has been greatly reduced. The plan is to maintain the current state of the civil industry and focus on the military industry.

The military industry is currently unable to meet the needs of the army. The ones that we originally had were weak, and under the raids of the illegal empire, it is difficult to expand our military industry soon. According to the report from the National Security Department (No. 11-A.2a), two feasible plans for the expansion of the military industry by exploiting the EEMD Jurisdiction are as follows:
1. Raid the Empress Cozy Glow’s arsenal: It is expected to immediately replenish the military equipment gap.
2. Infiltrate the military factory in Saint Glow Town: It is expected to obtain their lathes and machines.

Apart from this, in terms of resources, the Crystal Mountain Exploration Team reported that a large amount of crystal ore has been discovered in the Crystal Mountains, and there seems to be buildings built by ponies. A large exploration team is planned to be sent to the Crystal Mountains to execute the development plan, which is expected to take one month.

Signature: Head of Economy, Sugar Belle

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_24_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_25]
A Leaking Net

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_25_desc]
Inside the Joint Command Headquarters, Party Favor was pointing at the map and discussing the raid plan against the EEMD Jurisdiction. According to Report 27-B.0a, he needed to plan the routes to Empress Cozy Glow’s arsenal and the military factory in Saint Glow Town. Therefore, he called a meeting. Acting Head of Navy, Feather Bangs, and Acting Head of Airforce, Night Glider, were present. Double Diamond, the Head of Security, was absent due to border affairs.

When asked about the defense situation in the EEMD, Night Glider spoke first, “I have to say, these soldiers in the EEMD are like they are on a field trip. I flew around and saw that there are more than a dozen outposts within a ten-mile radius, but over half of them are empty! They are less threatening than the potholes on the road.”

Feather Bangs, although acting as the Acting Head of Navy, was originally from the Army, so he had something to say when he went on a mission with the Army, “That’s not all. The border patrols stationed at the outposts are mostly drinking all day. Some even fight with the reconnaissance pegasi. I have to say, it’s quite a spectacle!”

“Ha! I bet crossing their border is as easy as going home. It’s a pity that we can’t have a large-scale operation to avoid the troops of Cozy Glow.”

Party Favor then asked, “What about the arsenal and the military factory? I guess they are as ‘well-defended’ as the border?”

Night Glider replied, “Indeed, Feather Bangs and I have checked them. There is almost no defense at both places. The garrison is either eating or sleeping, with almost no threat.”

Party Favor thought for a moment and then jumped in excitement, “I’ve got a plan! The operation will be carried out at night. Feather Bangs and I will take a team to deal with the guards and patrols. Night Glider will take the pegasi to empty the arsenal or the machines before dawn. Remember to be quick!”

“What if they find out that things are missing when it’s daylight?”

“You mean Snips and Snails? With their cowardice, they will probably tell Cozy Glow that they ‘lost them during transportation.’”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_25_o0]
The three ponies laughed together in cheerful atmosphere.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_26]
The Sequel

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_26_desc]
Our town has a very different atmosphere from Ponyville. As Wandering Wind walked down the street, he saw earth ponies, pegasi, and unicorns walking together, chatting and laughing, instead of a few earth ponies bullying a unicorn like in Ponyville. The weather here is not as cold as Ponyville, and it is mostly sunny here, instead of snowing every day. More importantly, there are no imperial ponies here.

Wandering Wind recalled Ponyville many years ago, when Princess Twilight Sparkle still lived there, when Cozy Glow was a foolish kid who knew nothing but playing with mud, when there were no conflicts among the three tribes. It was a good time in Ponyville. It’s really strange! Starlight Glimmer and Trixie Lulamoon were even good friends back then. If only he had asked Starlight Glimmer to execute Trixie Lulamoon back then...

Suddenly, ponies around him scattered. He looked up and saw the damn imperial reconnaissance pegasi. How dare these bastards fly here? A surge of anger rose from Wandering Wind’s heart. He picked up a brick and threw it with all his might at one of the pegasi, hitting him right in the head. The pegasi was hit hard and couldn’t even fly straight. His companion had to help him back home in a hilarious way.

“Wow, that was amazing! What a nice shot! You beat them up so neatly!” Wandering Wind turned around and saw Fervent Flame in the air, holding a crossbow and shouting. “With such accuracy, why not you join us and beat the hell out of those imperial fools! What do you think?”

Wandering Wind remembered those hateful things again: his apple orchard, his home, Ponyville, the riot police... Suddenly, he thought of Trixie Lulamoon. How could a little magician dare to destroy everything of his? Thinking of her, Wandering Wind felt a little nauseous and inevitably a little angry.

“Of course, I hate the empire. Let’s go back to Ponyville and capture Trixie Lulamoon alive!” He paused for a moment. “But what should I do? The conscription office seems to have been abandoned for a long time and is about to become a ruin.”

“No pony would want to conscript under the noses of the reconnaissance pegasi. The conscription office is a key target of the reconnaissance pegasi. But it doesn’t matter! Beating up the empire is not illegal. As long as you want, I’ll go tell Magenta Mist. Why not go to our place? We can go together. The more ponies, the stronger we are.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_26_o0]
“No problem.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_27]
Night Operation: Empress Mountain

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_27_desc]
At midnight, ponies in the EEMD Jurisdiction were free from anxiety and entered a happy dream. Even the border patrol ponies in the guard post, instead of making the difficult decision to guard or patrol at night, resolutely chose to sleep to make up for their idleness during the day.

Most of the guard ponies at the Empress Mountain Arsenal were asleep, and a few ponies who had eaten too much during the day were playing cards outside. “Pair!” “Set!” “Quad!”... The loud noises of the game were heard one after another. When the last voice of “Royal flush! I win, give me all the money in the pot!” was heard, music came from the bushes nearby. The pony who won the game was still happy to have music to celebrate his victory. A few seconds later, the other ponies realized something was wrong and looked towards the bushes. The next second, several balloons flew from behind and hit the back of their heads accurately.

After the guards “fell asleep”, Party Favor and Feather Bangs led their respective teams out of the bushes on both sides. After confirming that there were no guards around, Party Favor released a balloon to the mountain far away to inform Night Glider, then asked Feather Bangs, who was holding a radio, “Nice music, what song is it?” “It’s the victory settlement music of ‘Pegasus Hold’em’. It doesn’t feel exciting enough. Ha! How about changing it to ‘In Our Town’ next time?” “Come on, aren’t you afraid that Starlight Glimmer will beat you up? Wait, maybe you can sneak into the Canterlot Palace and throw the radio at Cozy Glow’s bedside to scare her to death in the middle of the night!”

The ponies present laughed until Night Glider and the pegasi arrived. The ponies entered the arsenal through the gate that wasn’t even closed.

“Wow, so many weapons, enough to supply us for quite a while.” Night Glider said, asking the pegasi to transport the supplies back to Our Town. Feather Bangs and a team of ponies were counting the number of supplies on the side. He couldn’t help but rubbish the imperial ponies, “What a waste to give them these things. They even put wands in the gun barrels? It even feels like they are trying to just gift us equipments on the battlefield. Kind-hearted, huh?”

“Have you ever seen a radio like this? There’s a big ‘push to talk’ button on it. They can’t even distinguish between a walkie-talkie and a radio? Or is this some kind of hybrid?” Party Favor threw the mutated radio into the bushes outside. “Okay, let’s move quickly. It will be dawn soon.”

The ponies worked hard for several hours. By the time of dawn, the ponies had completed their mission and returned to Our Town. The half-closed gate concealed the “flew away” weapons, until a border patrol discovered the missing equipment and couldn’t go on patrol. Our Town was particularly peaceful that day.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_27_o0]
Thanks for the hospitality!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_28]
Night Operation: Saint Glow Town

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_28_desc]
The night fell, in a dark alley in Saint Glow Town, a few unicorns were blocking the earth pony Alfred, because this new pony did not pay the “factory entrance fee”.

Alfred fell to the ground, flashbacks of his life covered his eyes, temporarily taking him away from the darkness in front of him: he was originally a fugitive. He was so close to crossing the border, only to run into the border patrol. His companion was lucky enough to run into a forest, but he failed. After being caught, he was sentenced to fifty years of work for the empire. He was assigned to the military factory in Saint Glow Town. The factory manager was also a bastard, using ponies as slaves just to meet his quota...

“Bang!” Alfred was kicked right in the face. It’s rumored that these unicorns in front of him bribed the factory manager to become junior managers. And with the protection of the manager, they are now extorting their subordinates without any scruples. They saw Alfred, the new comer, the one who was sentenced, and an earth pony, so they naturally made up a reason “not paying the entrance fee” to block him in the alley and rob him. “Who do you think you are? If you don’t pay the entrace fee, you totally deserve this!” Another kick hit Alfred. Suddenly, he felt powerless. The bag he was holding fell to the ground, and they took it away. “Remember, tomorrow the same place... or else...” Alfred couldn’t hear what they said next, as the buzzing in his head was too loud.

After some time, Alfred woke up from his coma. He felt a sharp pain all over his body. He tried to get up, but a shadow covered him. It was a small gray pony at the exit of the alley, staring at him.

“Wow! You are lying in this dark alley, and you are seriously injured. That’s really bad. What happened?” Hearing this, Alfred replied, “...It was a few factory security guards. They robbed me and...” Alfred suddenly realized that the pony in front of him was exactly the same as the one called Party Favor in the empire’s wanted poster. “You! You are...!”

“You recognize me? Yes, I am a member of the resistance.” Party Favor said in a relaxed tone, “It’s okay to report me. What will the ponies in the EEMD do? They can tell what you are by the bruises on your body. Besides, I advise you not to look back. A crossbow is aiming at you right now.” Alfred dared not move. He was afraid that the pony from the resistance would order to shoot him with a crossbow and pierce his head. “Please, don’t kill me. I don’t want to die. I want to go back...” Alfred thought of his hometown, thought of Trixie Lulamoon, and he is increasingly melting down. “I have no home...”

“Maybe, but if you can tell us how to get into the military factory —” Actually, Party Favor knew how to get in, he just wanted to confirm that Alfred is not one of those obedient ponies who would work for the empire for the rest of his life, but someone who has a little resistance against the empire. “Just now! They are the factory managers. They have the keys!” The desire to survive occupied Alfred’s brain. He just wanted to live, no matter what the cost.

“Oh, thank you for helping us!” Party Favor left the alley slowly, giving Alfred a look of “well done” before leaving. Alfred was left alone in the alley, his thoughts even more chaotic: helping the resistance, this is already considered treason, and he may be sentenced to death for treason... Why is it that in the end, it’s all about death? Not helping the resistance will lead to death, helping will lead to death, he just wanted to live, but fate has laid two dead ends for him — he fell silent, sat in the alley, looked up at the rotating starry sky, and quietly waited for his fate.

There were pegasi in the sky carrying something back and forth. They must be the ponies from the resistance, right? Anyway, it has nothing to do with me, Alfred thought. Until the last group of pegasi flew eastward, they dropped something — it was Alfred’s wallet, without a single bit missing, and a note attached — “Don’t give up, the resistance is with you”. Alfred widened his eyes, put the wallet in his bag, stood up, and left the alley without looking back.

The next day, the entire management of the military factory went crazy, frantically looking for which pony below dared to be so bold and dared to touch their things. Alfred kept his mouth shut about the resistance’s actions. They found nothing in the end, and had to report “lost during relocation”. They didn’t dare to say that it was the ponies from the east who did it, just as Party Favor had guessed.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_28_o0]
Seed is planted, waiting for it to sprout...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_29]
A New Era

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_29_desc]
Double Diamond sat in the office, looking at the report that was intercepted by the reconnaissance pegasi, feeling a little annoyed: Night Glider has been out nine times a day, and the messenger was intercepted. Don’t these reconnaissance pegasi need to rest?

He couldn’t stand it anymore, glanced at the clock, and decided to go to the research institute immediately. But as soon as he went out, he saw several reconnaissance pegasi holding a wand and diving towards the ground. “Run!” Double Diamond had a bad feeling, and those pegasi were already flying towards him. It wasn’t until a brick suddenly flew and hit one of the pegasi’s head that the rest of the pegasi gave up diving and flew back to their base in cloudsdale.

Double Diamond’s anger grew, and he rushed to the research institute at the fastest speed, knocking on the door: “Starlight Glimmer, Sunburst, where is the promised radio?!”

“Hey! What are you doing?” Sunburst looked at the blueprints blown away by the opened door. “Well, the radio is ready, but there is a problem, it can’t be started.” He pointed to the radio with the extinguished indicator light.

“What? My messages are intercepted every day, and myself almost got intercepted just now. Now you say the radio is broken? I want to see what’s going on!” Double Diamond walked to the radio and glanced at it, kicked it with anger.

“Hey! You...” Sunburst was about to stop him, but the indicator light on the radio suddenly “beeped!” and lit up. “Wow...”

“At least he can be used now! Okay, give me a few radios, I’m leaving!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_29_o0]
A New Era of Communication

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_30]
Communication Restored

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_30_desc]
The Day of Contact is here once again, the radio was finally put into use after being “repaired” by Sunburst and Double Diamond. The United Resistance can finally communicate safely without having the messenger go through levels of danger just to deliver a letter.

Starlight sat in front of the radio, tuned the radio to the frequency that only the modified radio could receive, and pressed the call button: “This is Starlight Glimmer, Sunset Shimmer, do you copy? Repeat. Do you copy?”

“This is Sunset Shimmer, Affirmative. Over.” Sunset Shimmer changed her tone again: “Seriously, why can’t we just talk normally, like we used to?”

“Well, that makes sense. So what about Discord? Can he hear us?” Starlight finished speaking, and a sound similar to a prompt tone came from the other end of the microphone: “Beep — beep, the number you dial is currently busy, please try again later.”

“Discord? Busy? What’s going on?” “Oh — Miss Starlight, I am currently talking to you, of course I am in a call, can’t you figure that out?”

“Discord!!” “Discord Radio? That’s a great idea! I will consider changing ‘Starlight Radio’ to ‘Discord Radio’. Anyway, everything is normal here, we are about to use this to beat the crap out of Cozy Glow, over!”

“Hey!!!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_30_o0]
“One of communication and Discord is normal”, Sunset Shimmer said.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_30_o1]
“Hey! This is way better than banana phones!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_30_o2]
“One of communication and Discord is normal”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_31]
Unexpected Discovery

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_31_desc]
After the Economic Department issued the order to explore the Crystal Cave, a large exploration team was formed. A group of ponies with strong abilities in exploration, scientific research, logistics, etc., temporarily left their jobs and prepared for this important exploration plan. Only the soldiers are unable to participate due to the pressure of the empire’s attack. Anyway, the Economic Department recruited a group of refugees who are good at fighting and have no job to join the exploration team to replace the soldiers. Wandering Wind is also among them. He and more than a dozen other ponies serve as the defense force to protect the safety of the exploration team.

As they entered the valley, the surrounding environment changed dramatically. Behind them was a lush plain, while the road leading to the cave ahead was completely different: the terrain was undulating, covered with a layer of ice and snow from top to bottom. Strangely, once all the ice and snow passed that boundary, they melted into water and flowed into a stream in the blink of an eye. There is no doubt that this is the influence of magic crystals. The magic power of the crystals here is so high that it overflows. This is a good sign! It means that the crystals here must be of high quality...

But as they went further up, the magic power became more and more bizarre — especially at the entrance of the cave, all the unicorns in the team suddenly regained their magic power! Some of the unicorns can even use advanced magic such as magic beams. The ponies were very excited, especially the scientists in the team — they may have found a way to restore magic power! Soon, the exploration team was divided into different groups, and the group responsible for exploration quickly advanced towards the cave, investigating the crystal deposits and the magic contained in the crystals.

Wandering Wind and his group are responsible for protecting the safety of the base camp and exploring the surrounding terrain. Ahead of them is a valley, with high mountains on both sides and the Crystal Cave in between. As they walked forward along the valley, some exposed crystals appeared on the roadside, but the road ahead suddenly stopped: an unusual mountain stood up in the middle of the valley, cutting off the otherwise natural valley road, making it extremely discordant. Wandering Wind walked towards the mountain, and when he was ten meters away from the foot of the mountain, he sensed that something was wrong — he seemed to be walking in place, no matter how hard he tried to move forward, as if a gust of invisible wind was pushing him out.

As if being shielded, the area in front seemed to be frozen in time. Wandering Wind was frightened and quickly ran towards the exit of the valley. He hadn’t run far when he was tripped by the exposed crystal. He got up and dared not stay here any longer. Just as he was about to run, he saw a beam of light in front of him — the crystal he tripped over changed the angle and reflected the sunlight. The beam of light kept reflecting in the surrounding crystals, and finally shot towards the mountain. A ripple echoed on the barrier that blocked Wandering Wind before, and then the entire mountain disappeared in front of him. In its place was a strange-looking building emitting a strange light arc —

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_31_o0]
Report the Research Department immediately!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_31_TOOLTIP]
§RWhat is this...?§!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_32]
Science Nexus

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_32_desc]
After the news from the Crystal Mountain exploration team reached Our Town, the entire Research Department was in total excitement: What is this place? Why is there a whole mountain and a barrier protecting it? Is it the work of Star Swirl the Bearded? Or is there another pony behind it? To protect this secret, the National Security Department has recalled the entire exploration team and placed them under observation. The agents have sealed off the area, and the production operation of the Crystal Cave can only be resumed after the investigation is completed.

Sunburst fervently went on a trip to the Crystal Mountain to investigate the secret behind this wonder. According to the clues provided by a pony named Wandering Wind in the exploration team, Sunburst’s team found the valley. By moving a piece of crystal, the entire mountain along with the barrier slowly disappeared, revealing the building, the secret hidden by the mountain.

The main part of the building is a spire, similar to the Crystal Castle of the Crystal Empire. There is a ring-shaped building around it, which has been severely damaged, and its fragments are scattered on the surrounding ground. There are no crystals here, but unicorns can use magic normally.

Through the hole in the large ring, the ponies entered the spire and began to explore the castle separately, hoping to find some information or books. This is truly a treasure trove of science and magic: rearch documents here are comparable to the Canterlot Library, and there is even some knowledge that has never been recorded in the Canterlot Library.

Lost in the ocean of knowledge, Sunburst passed through the door leading to the central area of the spire and entered the core of the entire spire. There was almost nothing there, only a crystal column standing in the center. Like the Crystal Heart, a dim crystal orb floated in the middle of the crystal column. Suddenly, as if receiving some kind of guidance, Sunburst walked towards the crystal orb, aimed his horn at it, and started casting magic on it.

The dim crystal orb suddenly emitted a purple light, and a beam of light spread out from the crystal orb, making the surrounding walls transparent. Through the transparent walls, Sunburst saw a miracle happening outside: the broken ring was lifted into the air, and its fragments were returning to their original positions, repairing the large ring. When the last piece was in place, the edge of the ring flashed white light, and the entire ring began to rotate around the spire. A circular table appeared in the core of the spire, like the cutie map in Twilight’s Castle. Many bookshelves appeared around the room, all recording knowledge that Sunburst had never heard of:

Lost Science

The map revealed words, telling Sunburst the secret of this place: this crystal orb — the “Heart of Knowledge”, is the source of magic in the entire area. It can control the switch of the barrier, allowing the ponies inside to see the outside in one direction, while from the outside, there is only a mountain protecting this place — the Science Nexus. This is the reason why this place has not been discovered by ponies for thousands of years. The Science Nexus, the Heart of Knowledge, and the knowledge of mysticism... Sunburst has a lot to sort out, but now, what he is thinking about is —

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_32_o0]
What a perfect base...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_33]
Joke Collection

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_33_desc]
Cozy Glow was worried that her reputation among the people was not very good, so she disguised herself as an ordinary pony and randomly asked the ponies passing by on the street.
She asked a pony, “What do you think of Empress Cozy Glow?” The pony was shocked after hearing this, quickly pulled Cozy into a nearby alley, looked around to make sure there were no eavesdroppers, and finally said:
“Let me tell you secretly, I support Empress Cozy Glow.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_33_o0]
Thanks for listening!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_34]
Report 13-A.0a

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_34_desc]
Subject: The Crystal Empire

After the signing of the Canterlot Pact, the Crystal Empire was forced to comply with many unreasonable demands from the illegal Equestria Empire and the Changeling Empire: the PACT stipulates that the Crystal Empire must be demilitarized, subject to the illegal empire, and its government is managed by the illegal empire. The Changeling Empire claims to guarantee the independence of the Crystal Empire, while demanding that the Crystal Empire provide love tribute. The Crystal Empire has become a de facto colony of the illegal empire and the Changeling Empire.

The Crystal Empire has a council, the main forces of which are as follows:
- Equestria Unity Commission: composed of representatives sent by the illegal empire, representing the interests of Canterlot, and manipulating council elections.
- Changeling Consultants Delegate: composed of representatives sent by the Changeling Empire, representing the interests of the Changelings (Chrysalis).
- Crystal Empire Council: composed of representatives of the Crystal Empire royal family, representing the interests of the royal family.
The secondary forces are as follows:
- Crystal Empire Harmonicist Party: composed of representatives of harmonism.
- Crystal Empire Liberation Party: composed of representatives of democracy.
- Red Crystal: composed of representatives of equatism.
Among them, the Royal Cabinet and the Harmonicist Party, the Liberation Party, and the Red Crystal have a certain anti- illegal empire and anti- Changeling Empire tendency. So they may develop into an opposition force.

The Canterlot Pact ruled that Princess Cadance was guilty of “war crimes”, punished her to abdicate, and confined her and Shining Armor in the Crystal Manor. Flurry Heart was proposed as the monarch of the Crystal Empire. The original royal supporters were mostly retained. Their political power is gradually recovering, but they have not yet been able to compete with the illegal empire and the Changeling Empire.
If the Crystal Empire has a direct conflict with the illegal empire or an accident occurs in the future, Princess Cadance will be an important force of harmonism and should be focused on and protected.

Signature: Head of Security, Double Diamond

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_34_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_35]
In the White Mist

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_35_desc]
Before the Ultimate Battle, residents in the Northeastern mountains were still trading occasionally with Our Town. But after the war, a snowstorm covered the road to the mountains in the east, and the ponies on the other side never came to Our Town again.

Since then, the ponies living in the east have become a mystery to the residents of Our Town. Now, taking the opportunity of a relatively warm season, Double Diamond plans to explore the mountains with his skiing equipment, hoping to contact the ponies on the other side. Even though the road to the east is still blocked by snow, the blizzard has stopped for now.

Fully prepared and equipped with a radio, Double Diamond sets off for the east. He arrives at the cave where he once chased Starlight Glimmer. The entrance to the cave is blocked by snow again, so he props up his ski poles and climbs to the top of the mountain ahead, trying to find traces of pony life in the mountains. When he reaches the top of the mountain, Double Diamond looks to the east: there are continuous mountains covered with snow several meters high. At the end of the white snow, there seems to be a plain, or maybe a forest, hidden in the bleak white mist, which he cannot see clearly.

At least the ponies are not hiding in the snow several meters high in the mountains, Double Diamond thinks to himself, and reports to the radio: “This is Double Diamond. Behind the cave, there are many mountains covered with snow about three meters high. It seems that there is a plain in the distance, but I don’t know if there are any traces of ponies living.”
On the other end of the radio is Starlight Glimmer, who replies: “This is Starlight Glimmer. If possible, move towards the plain and remember, safety first.”

Double Diamond puts down his sled and slides down from the mountaintop, heading further east. The snow in the valley is whiter than anything else, and if it weren’t for the occasional gray boulders reminding Double Diamond that he was really moving forward, he might have thought he was standing still. After who knows how many hours, Double Diamond finally leaves the undulating white and gray and slides into the white and green.

The temperature in the forest is very low, and the surrounding mist makes it difficult for Double Diamond to see the road. As he walks through the forest, he suddenly bumps into a wooden table: there are ponies living here! Double Diamond is very excited, and this discovery is not in vain after several hours of effort. He immediately picks up the radio and shouts: “This is Double Diamond! I found a place where ponies live. It seems to be a village ahead!”

“Really? Hurry, hurry and look forward, contact the villagers there!” Double Diamond immediately packs up his equipment and walks towards the village.

Although there are traces of pony life, the village becomes more and more strange: their well is full of snow, the snow on the table has not been cleaned for a long time, and the surroundings become more and more gloomy. Especially with the white mist lingering around Double Diamond, the village exudes an ominous atmosphere. Fortunately, the mist seems to be dissipating soon. Double Diamond has not encountered a single pony. He walked to the front of one of the houses, knocked on the door, only to find that the door was ajar. Double Diamond walked into the house, and suddenly, his eyes widened: the pony inside, sitting on a stool, was covered with a thin layer of frost, and had become an ice sculpture.

Double Diamond was shocked. He stumbled out of the room, and the mist outside had dissipated. He saw the ponies in the mist: some were standing on the ground, looking up at the sky. Some were lying on the ground with their eyes closed. There was also a mother, holding her child in her arms, leaning peacefully against a wooden stake. They had all turned into ice sculptures, vividly as if they were still alive. This scene made Double Diamond panic, and he quickly opened his backpack and grabbed the radio: “Starlight Glimmer, Starlight Glimmer! This is Double Diamond. I saw the villagers here, they are standing in the center of the village, they have... they have all turned into ice sculptures, they are all frozen to death!!”

“What did you say?!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_35_o0]
Rest in peace, we have finally learned of your fate...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_36]
Sinister Trade

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_36_desc]
As with every day of the past three years, Starlight Glimmer is dealing with the affairs of the Resistance. From time to time she looks at the map, organizes her thoughts and information in an attempt to find a way to strike back at the illegal empire.

“Starlight Glimmer, a new wave of refugees has arrived in Our Town. We are about to help them settle down, and Sugar Belle is waiting for you there.” Double Diamond reminds Starlight Glimmer. “Okay, let’s go.” More and more refugees are arriving, and Our Town may not be able to accommodate so many refugees. Perhaps some of the refugees should be settled in Suburst Farm or Northern Hooflyn. Starlight Glimmer picks up her bag and prepares to go to help settle the refugees and see if there are any other areas that can help Our Town share the pressure.

The center of Our Town is crowded with many newly arrived refugees, including those who have traveled from Canterlot, Ponyville, and the Crystal Empire... Some of them are seriously injured, which must have been done by the patrol. Starlight Glimmer sees a pink pony running towards her in a hurry: it is Sugar Belle, who seems to be covered in sweat, with a look of shock and a hint of anger on her face.

“Starlight Glimmer! I just helped a pony who came from Manehattan settle down. I can’t believe what Gladmane has done to them!”

“A pony from Manehattan? What did Gladmane do?” Starlight Glimmer checks her memory and finds that there were no refugees from Manehattan before. Strange, what has Gladmane done? This pony from Manehattan must know something...

“He said Gladmane’s ponies kidnapped his family and threatened them to work in a mine. The foreman didn’t let them rest, and... they were sold!”

Starlight Glimmer’s eyes widened when she heard the great evil in Manehattan, a concept she had only heard of in stories: “Sold as... a slave?!”

“It sounds like it... Gladmane obviously treats ponies as commodities, selling them to the bigwigs in Manehattan, Fillydelphia, and Baltimare.” Sugar Belle guesses based on the information provided by the pony from Manehattan.

“How dare he... this must have something to do with Cozy.” In her anger, Starlight Glimmer suddenly had an idea. “Double Diamond, this is an opportunity. We can use this as a chance to liberate the ponies in Manehattan who are in dire straits. The National Security Department should now go collect more information about Manehattan and report it to me. We need to take action.”

“No problem.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_36_o0]
So that’s the “prosperity” the illegal empire claimed...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_36_TOOLTIP]
§REnough is enough§!
Unlock national focuses related to §YManehattan Raid§!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_37]
Manehattan Raid

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_37_desc]
The broadcast from Our Town spread throughout Equestria, with the Resistance leader Starlight Glimmer accusing Manehattan of “conducting evil slave trade”. At the same time, she sent troops to the Manehattan Business Alliance.

Mayor Gladmane of Manehattan defended that “all trades in Manehattan are normal business activities”, while the Equestria Empire, which has nominal jurisdiction over the Manehattan area, has been widely questioned. Empress Cozy Glow was asked to “provide a reasonable explanation for the situation in Manehattan”.

The following content is reprinted from “Starlight Radio”:
“Today, with anger in our hearts, we have to reveal an unfortunate fact: Manehattan, a city once proud of its bustling streets and multiculturalism, has secretly become the breeding ground for the dark empire of Gladmane.”

“Gladmane and his gang once advertised ‘we will give every pony a job’, but in reality, the ponies received no wages and were forced to work for their masters. Gladmane’s gang treats ordinary ponies as commodities, defining the dignity and value of ponies with money. Those ponies who were once free and full of hope are now trapped in a nightmare of slavery. Their dreams are crushed, their spirits are broken, and they are now just pawns in Gladmane’s twisted game. It is a cruel twist of fate that has turned a city known for its bright lights into a stage of tragedy and heartbreak.”

“The stories told by those who managed to escape this terrible fate are as chilling as the winter wind. They talk about a life deprived of dignity, struggling under the watchful eyes of their supervisors. This is a stark reminder: in a land of friendship and harmony, there are ponies who exploit the weak for their own benefit.”

“The forces that allow Gladmane’s gang to commit crimes are led by the boss of all crimes, no other than Empress Cozy Glow. Now, in front of all the ponies in Equestria, she has allowed slave trade in her so-called ‘Equestria Empire’! Cozy Glow has planned dirty trade deals, and her name will be nailed to the pin of shame in Equestria history, to be despised and ridiculed for generations to come.”

“The evil deeds of the Business Alliance have been exposed, and the citizens of Equestria demand justice. The Resistance will not tolerate such evil deeds, and Gladmane must pay the price for his actions!”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_37_o0]
Well, the Empire has to make some statement.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_37_o1]
Advance!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_37_o2]
What?!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_38]
For Freedom

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_38_desc]
The camera freezes on the streets of Fillydelphia. A layer of snow covers the streets of Fillydelphia, dyeing the entire road white. The freed ponies gathered by the shop windows on the side of the street, waiting for the screens inside the windows to show the picture.

The camera switches to Manehattan. The prosperity of the Bridleway Building is still there, but the former owner has long since fled. Among the high-rise buildings, thousands of ponies look up at the big screen, waiting for an inspiring message.

The camera returns to Our Town. Starlight Glimmer sits in front of the camera, and today, she will take an important step in the cause of liberation — announcing the establishment of the Equestria Liberation Front. She took a last look at the speech, took a deep breath, opened the camera, and spoke with the Canterlot Royal accent that Twilight Sparkle taught her years ago:

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_38_o0]
“To all our friends around the world...”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39]
Establishment of the Front

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39_desc]
A sudden change happened in the Eastern Equestria. Today, Starlight Glimmer announced the establishment of the Equestria Liberation Front, and declared the current regime, the Equestria Empire, as “illegal, and disgusting”, and the Liberation Front as “the only legitimate government of Equestria”.

Empress Wuxuguang of the Equestria Empire responded to this, saying that “This is intolerable treason, the Liberation Front is totally unjust” and began to increase the troops on the border with the Liberation Front. It seems that a war between the two sides will break out in the near future...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39_o0]
We are the Orthodox!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39_o1]
Ponie’s Army!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39_o2]
Good luck, Starlight Glimmer

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_39_o3]
Civil war time?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_40]
Mission Failed

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_40_desc]
The Empire has requested us to send troops to Baltimare to stabilize the area and prevent Starlight Glimmer from further controlling the area - and we failed. Our troops did not arrive in Baltimare in time, and the road to Baltimare was unobstructed. The Empire had to send troops from Canterlot urgently with night marches to arrive in Baltimare before Starlight Glimmer’s troops.

That day, Empress Cozy Glow was furious on the phone, and the officials of Ponyville were scolded by the Empress for more than an hour. “I don’t want to hear any excuses, I don’t want to hear any reasons, your failure has disappointed me greatly! You bunch of useless idiots, wait for your punishment! I want all of you... No... No matter how you are punished, it is not enough to compensate for the losses caused to the Empire by your negligence! The entire Ponyville will pay the price for your inaction!”

“Compensation... Empress, are you interested in Ponyville Day Spa Mane Care Vouchers by any chance?” A Ponyville official tried to break the awkward silence, and he succeeded, the phone was hung up.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_40_o0]
Oh, no...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_41]
EEMD Under Attack

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_41_desc]
(Ringring, ringring...)
“...Snips, Snails, is it you?”

“Yes, yes, Your Majesty...”

“I heard that there were some ‘impostors’ in your juridiction, the Ministry of Friendship have reported to me, do you know?”

“Your Majesty, they are not the Resistance, they are just a few thieves, they have been... they have been caught!”

“Organized, disciplined ‘thieves’ huh? Interesting, very interesting... Can you come up with better stories?”

“Emm...”

“Well, I am a kind soverign, who values friendship, So that’s why I will forgive you... ok?”

“Thank you, Your Majesty! We will...”

“In your dreams! You two dumbasses! You are the ministers of Defence, and you can’t even guard a small segment of border! How can you ignore my orders?! You deceive me, and everything you do is just dragging me down! Look out of your window, if I ever see another rebel from the Resistance in your jurisdiction, you two will become the next Twilight Sparkle! Understand?”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_41_o0]
Which side are they even on?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_42]
Southeastern Equestria Uprising

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_42_desc]
Since the war began, all security forces have been rushing to the northern front. The uprising forces in the southern region of the Business Alliance have thus continued to grow and develop.

Under the secret push of our Security Department, the resistance forces in these areas launched an uprising today to cooperate with the northern offensive.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_42_o0]
United for Victory

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_43]
Escape From Manehattan

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_43_desc]
Recently, the famous Manehattan writer Makita Hayanov published the prologue of the test version of the novel series “Escape From Manehattan”, depicting a world line where Manehattan is in chaos to the readers.

The story takes place in Manehattan after the collapse of the Gladmane Group. The Empire’s blockade of Manehattan has led to chaos in Manehattan, and the ponies are trapped on this island. The protagonist Makita is a soldier of the Empire, whose mother was sold to Manehattan because of the slave trade. He therefore signed up to join the Empire’s peacekeeping force stationed in Manehattan. However, he was abandoned by the Empire and trapped in Manehattan.

To escape from Manehattan, Makita was forced to fight with and against four different forces. The author portrayed vivid characters, such as the former security force officer who puts business above all else, the logistics officer of the peacekeeping force who is driven by interests, the gang network that spreads throughout Manehattan, and the two brothers Killa and Tagilla who occupy the mall and chemical factory... The work was warmly welcomed by readers around the world once it was published. As of now, the sales have exceeded tens of thousands. To express his gratitude, Makita announced that he will publish the official version of “Escape From Manehattan” in the near future, and affectionately referred to the readers as “true believers”.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_43_o0]
Can’t wait for the official release!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_44]
Rarity’s Boutique

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_44_desc]
In the center of Manehattan, there is a small, insignificant shop. Its original sign has been obscured by a wooden board. The board vaguely reveals a few words, which are difficult to discern. For years, the nearby residents have come to collect food and relief supplies every day, so that in the memories of the ponies, this place seems like a relief station. Well, three years ago, it was called “Rarity’s Boutique”.

After the Ultimate Battle, tens of thousands of ponies fled to Manehattan from the west. At that time, the streets of Manehattan were crowded with refugees, traffic was paralyzed, and order was chaotic. At that time, Manehattan was like a basin at the end of the valley in the face of the flood from the west, and the entire society would collapse at any moment. The shop assistant of Rarity’s Boutique, Coco Pommel, was unable to contact Rarity, so she closed the door of the shop and prayed that the chaos outside would not spread to this peaceful place.

The chaos lasted until Gladmane became the mayor of Manehattan. Overnight, this insignificant shop witnessed all the ponies on the streets of Manehattan becoming the private property of the Gladmane Group. Chaos disappeared, at the price of a new order taking its place. Container after container of ponies were shipped out of Manehattan, and the ponies left in Manehattan became the consumables of the big companies. Residential buildings were transformed into beehives, carrying more than eight times the designed capacity of ponies. The food supply was so low, that the ponies are almost at the point of cannibalism.

Coco Pommel did not want to see such a tragedy, so she take up the job of clothing design and reopened the shop. By providing custom clothing for the executives of those big companies, Coco Pommel earned the license to operate, and with the profits from the carefully designed clothing, she was able to afford sufficient food and daily necessities. Coco covered the sign “Rarity’s Boutique” with a wooden board to avoid attracting attention from the Empire’s secret police. From then on, this clothing store transformed into a relief station that distributed relief supplies to residents and slaves.

When Manehattan was liberated, when the ponies no longer had to rely on relief to survive, the relief station had finally completed its mission. Coco Pommel removed the wooden board covering the sign, and “Rarity’s Boutique” reappeared in the sight of the ponies, resuming its original business.

Unfortunately, the owner of this shop is no longer with us.

Fortunately, Manehattan still remembers her.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_44_o0]
Salute

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_45]
Reckoning

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_45_desc]
Inside a tavern in Fillydelphia, ponies are discussing their future after breaking free from the slave trade — except one of them is not. His face is gloomy, he wears a large hat, an oversized coat, sunglasses, and remains silent, afraid of being recognized.

Lighting in the tavern is temporarily out of order, making the corner too dark for any pony to sit next to him. Ten minutes later, another pony covered in hoodie and sunglasses sits next to him and starts talking: “These ponies... all they celebrate is the arrival of the Resistance, but never the ones who gave them jobs.”

Hearing this, the pony in the corner suddenly turned his head, realizing that the pony next to him is also a pony who wants to escape to Baltimare, finally, a companion! “Yeah, these ungrateful ponies!” he complained.

“Looks like you’re going to Baltimare, too?” the hoodie pony asked.

“Of course, I made so much effort to take over the Canterlot Restaurant on Main Street, and those rascals just took it away. I have nothing left in Manehattan, so I have to go to Baltimare.”

He took a sip of his drink and asked the pony in the hoodie, “So what about you? Why are you going to Baltimare?”

“I’m in a similar situation as you. Wait, you just mentioned Canterlot Restaurant, are you Rogers? The business genius who recently made it to the top of the Gladmane Group? I heard that your restaurant was doing so well, the revenue was skyrocketing. I’ve been wanting to meet you for a long time.” The pony in the hoodie suddenly became excited.

The alcohol kicked in, Rogers became more confident, “Ha! That’s me. Do you want my autograph? Experiences? Or business cooperation? Here, this is my business card, ordinary ponies don’t have the chance to get it. Wait, sorry... who are you again? Where are you from?”

The pony in the hoodie took off his sunglasses and smiled:

“I’m from the National Security Department of the Resistance, nice to meet you, Mr. Rogers.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_45_o0]
Lighting restored

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_46]
The Faithful Student

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_46_desc]
After Manehattan was liberated, the Liberation Front successfully resumed trade with the outside world. Canterlot is no longer able to interfere with the eastern ocean of the continent, so the maritime traffic line is very safe. The ports of the Manehattan and Horseshoe Bay are operating day and night, bringing products from Kirin, Seapony, and even Storm Island to the Liberation Front.

Now, Our Town is particularly lively. Thanks to the collapse of the economic blockade, resources from all over the south have poured into Our Town, and economic construction is in full swing.

A hippogriff flew from the southeast to Our Town, as if looking for somepony, until she saw Starlight Glimmer, and landed immediately.

“Principal Starlight!” She shouted to Starlight Glimmer, “I finally found you!”

Starlight Glimmer was startled by the sudden noise, turned around, and saw the source of the noise - Silverstream, a student of the previous School of Friendship.

“Silverstream? Wait, how did you get here?” Starlight Glimmer obviously didn’t expect Silverstream to appear in Our Town. “You should have returned to Seaquestria after the war, right?”

“Of course! I went back to Seaquestria, and when I heard that the Liberation Front was established, I wanted to come and help! Queen Novo also wanted me to come, but she was afraid of my safety. I persuaded her for a loooooooong time before I finally got on a ship and came here! I'm so happy to see you again!”

“Silverstream...” The students have not forgotten Starlight, nor have they forgotten friendship. Starlight Glimmer was so excited that she almost cried, but she held back her tears. “I didn’t expect you to come and help... Thank you, Silverstream, thank you so much.”

Silverstream was so happy that she could help Starlight Glimmer that she couldn’t stop herself from asking, “Hooray! So what about the other friends? Where are they?”

“I know Sandbar went to Storm Island and stayed with my friend Sunset. As for the other students... I haven’t been able to contact them yet. You are the only one who has come so far. But you coming here has helped me a lot, thank you, Silverstream!”

That day, the sea breeze from the south was particularly comfortable, bring good mood to the ponies, welcoming every day in the future.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_46_o0]
Power of Friendship

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_46_TOOLTIP]
Unlock decision: §YSupport from Seaquestria§!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47]
Liberation Front Border Action

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47_desc]
Military observers have recently noticed that the Liberation Front is deploying legions to the border with the Duchy of Ponyville. Given its scale, this is not a military exercise.

The situation on the border between the Liberation Front and Ponyville is becoming increasingly tense, and a large-scale conflict may erupt in the near future...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47_o0]
Are they finally going to act?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47_o1]
Soon...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47_o2]
Oh no...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_47_o3]
Okay

