[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_62]
April 22nd

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_62_desc]
It’s been a long time since I became a train driver and wrote a diary, but today I feel it’s necessary to record something.
This should be my last week in Las Pegasus. Together with Jackpot, we had a secret dinner with the assistants and other magicians from our magic show, and said goodbye. We are ready, and tomorrow we will leave here and go to Manehattan.
I took a few days off work, because I want to cherish this last week, to appreciate this place we once loved, the place where we ran our magic show for over a decade.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_62_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_62_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_63]
April 25th

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_63_desc]
The train is doing the final cargo transfer, and Jackpot has also sneaked onto the train. I had him disguise himself as a cargo handler, and no pony suspected anything.
I have been telling Jackpot all along that it was the Flim and Flam brothers who deceived us, that Mr. Gladmane was framed by them and forced out of Las Pegasus, which is why Las Pegasus has become what it is today. I can tell that Jackpot doesn’t believe me on this matter, but soon, I will be able to show him the splendor of Manehattan with his own eyes.
We heard that Mr. Gladmane not only has a thriving business in Manehattan, but has also become the mayor. When we arrive in Manehattan, we will visit him together. He might be able to help promote our magic show with his status as the mayor of Manehattan! Imagine the most luxurious upper-class ponies in the city of Manehattan go crazy for our show! But Jackpot seems to be indifferent to these things, he only cares about whether he can see his daughter in Ponyville. If he decides to quit the magic show business, I won’t blame him. After all, he didn’t say anything when I became a train driver.
The departure bell has already rung, that’s it, goodbye Las Pegasus! Hello, Manehattan!

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_63_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_63_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_63_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_64]
October 31st

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_64_desc]
Jackpot, I really hope you can see with your own eyes the prosperity of Manehattan. I have been living here for several months, and although I have not yet met Mr. Gladmane, I have already seen the prosperity of Manehattan.
The prosperity of Manehattan is really not the level that Los Pegasus, managed by those two scammers, can even compare to. Perhaps they have similar amounts of total wealth, but in Los Pegasus, all the wealth is only in the hooves of the twins; while here, wealth is in every shop on every street, in the wallets of every pony, and every pony has the opportunity to become rich.
I can see those noble ponies walking on the streets, their clothing is gorgeous, their smiles are bright, they travel between bars, theaters, and casinos, their lives are full of fun. Although I can’t be like them for the time being, because in the same accident when I lost you, I also lost all my savings. But I believe that as long as I continue to work hard, I will soon be able to become one of them.
When I first arrived in Manehattan, I couldn’t afford to rent a house, so I could only beg on the street. The streets of Manehattan are very clean, and there are hardly any ponies like me who are penniless. This once made me feel ashamed. But today, a kind employee of the Gladmane Group found me, he cared about me, and said that since I know Mr. Gladmane, he can definitely arrange a good job for me. He invited me to dinner at a restaurant, paid for my dinner, gave me a bed, and said he would take me directly to work tomorrow. I knew that Mr. Gladmane’s Manehattan would not allow any pony to be homeless on the street! I don’t know exactly what my new job will be, but it is said that I can also travel outside the city of Manehattan. I hope I can do my job well and not let them down.
Jackpot, look forward to the day when I will rise to the upper class of Manehattan! By then, I will return to magic performances, and I will make sure that all the ponies in Manehattan know your name!
In memory of my best friend and magic partner, Jackpot.

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_64_o0]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_64_o1]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_65]
You can recognize me, right?

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_65_desc]
The first ray of light in the morning can announce the end of the long night; however, it is not until the sun rises to the top of the head and the light is so strong that it is impossible to open the eyes, that the long night truly ends for the ponies who are waiting in long queues at the border to enter the empire.
At half past twelve noon, the border guards who had finished their lunch finally came lazily and slowly to the front, and began the entrance service for the day.
“Next! Papers please! Let me see... Your name is... Gladmane?"
The border guard raised his head in confusion and looked at the classy suit of the pony in front of him, together with muddy white hair that does not seem to match.

In the past, most of the ponies who went from here to the empire were poor ponies and the “full-time laborers” sent by the Gladmane Group; and recently, with the situation in Manehattan getting worse and worse, many wealthy ponies from the Group have fled to the empire.
But... there have been too many similar cases recently, some have stolen a set of classy suits from the mall, and some have even stolen a classy feather pen, trying to pretend to be wealthy ponies wanting to enter the empire. Anyway, Gladmane? He has his own palanquin and hot air balloon, why would he walk to the border?
The soldier was about to stamp the “denied entry” seal, when the pony in front seemed to notice the soldier’s suspicion and secretly handed over a handful of gold coins: “I really am Gladmane! My balloon was shot down by those crazy ponies in the city!”
The soldier took the gold coins and called his captain; the captain took more gold coins and called his officer.

The pony who claimed to be “Gladmane” saw the officer coming and immediately became excited. “Hey! I know you... You were in the security team of the Group before, right? Don’t remind me, let me think, your name is... eh... your name is... Damn what was it? Anyway, just let me pass, those blind idiots of yours don’t recognize me. You can recognize me, right?”
The officer looked up and down at the pony, then leaned over to his ear and whispered, “Yes, boss, I recognize you. It was you who transferred me from the most prosperous district of the Manehattan Group headquarters to this remote border inspection station that is in the middle of nowhere.”

The officer stepped back a few steps, and announced loudly to the soldiers, “I have seen Gladmane, but I don’t know who this pony is. Soldier, deny entry... no, wait, allow entry, and send all of them to the empire’s coal mine, this should be the last batch of ‘full-time laborers’ from Manehattan.”

[en.EVENT_C08_MAIN_65_o0]
He deserved

